<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
  <div class="text-center mb-16">
    <h1 class="font-serif font-light text-5xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-2">Recommendations</h1>
    <%= image_tag "flower-divider.png", alt: "", class: "h-8 w-auto mx-auto mt-2 mb-6" %>
    <p class="text-nasturtium-sage text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase">By City</p>
  </div>

  <%# ── BOULDER ── %>
  <div class="mb-20">
    <h2 class="font-serif font-light text-4xl text-nasturtium-forest-dark mb-4">Boulder</h2>
    <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed mb-10">
      We&rsquo;re excited to welcome everyone to Boulder on Friday evening to kick
      off the weekend! If you&rsquo;ve never been (or even if you have) we highly
      recommend having dinner in Boulder before the Welcome Drinks. There are a ton
      of great restaurants right along Pearl Street where the Welcome Drinks will
      be, and you can&rsquo;t beat the view of the Flatirons.
    </p>

    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-nasturtium-olive mb-5">Food</p>
    <div class="space-y-6 mb-10">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Mountain Sun Brewery</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          THE spot for casual vibes, super tasty food, incredible staff, and great
          beer. Maybe the best part &mdash; they still only take cash or check. Feels
          like the best of Colorado and what Pearl Street was like before Arc&rsquo;teryx
          and the like moved in across the street.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Avanti</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          A cool food hall right across from Oak at Fourteenth, our Welcome Drinks
          spot, that has a variety of food options, 2 bars, and an unbeatable
          rooftop with a view of the Flatirons.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Rosetta Hall</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Another great food hall option with a rooftop bar. It&rsquo;s slightly
          more upscale than Avanti.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">T/aco</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Cheap and very tasty tacos and margs with a laid back vibe. We try to go
          here whenever we get the chance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Decent Bagel</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          THE BEST BAGELS IN TOWN! Sunday morning after the wedding we&rsquo;ll meet
          in LaVern M. Johnson park in Lyons to share these bagels post the wedding
          but let&rsquo;s be real &mdash; one bagel the whole weekend isn&rsquo;t
          enough and we recommend visiting their NEW shop on Arapahoe Rd.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-nasturtium-olive mb-5">Bookstores</p>
    <div class="space-y-6 mb-10">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Boulder Bookstore</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          There forever. Big and perfect for walking through.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Trident Bookstore</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Cute little place with a great coffee shop inside.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-nasturtium-olive mb-5">Outdoors</p>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Boulder Bike Path + Boulder Creek</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Boulder is one of the most bikeable cities in the country! Much of the
          path runs along Boulder Creek and runs adjacent to downtown Boulder &amp;
          Pearl Street.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Chautauqua Park</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          A beautiful park south of Pearl Street that gets you up to the hiking
          trails that access the Flatirons.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Mount Sanitas</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          If you stay on Pearl Street for long enough, walking west, it&rsquo;ll turn
          into a hiking trail that&rsquo;ll get you high enough up for a quick view
          of just how flat Colorado is until the Flatirons that you&rsquo;re walking
          up pop out. It also connects to Mount Sanitas trail system.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── LYONS ── %>
  <div class="mb-20">
    <h2 class="font-serif font-light text-4xl text-nasturtium-forest-dark mb-4">Lyons</h2>
    <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed mb-10">
      Our wedding town! It&rsquo;s a lovely little town that gets you the feel of a
      Colorado mountain town without all the driving or elevation gain. As all great
      Colorado towns do, it has a lovely river path worth exploring.
    </p>

    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-nasturtium-olive mb-5">Food</p>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Moxie Bread Co.</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Local, small town bakery with delicious bread and pastries!
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Oskar Blues</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          The flagship location of the now national beer distributor that opened in
          1997. We&rsquo;ve heard they don&rsquo;t let you through security in Denver
          Airport if you didn&rsquo;t visit a brewery during your trip to Colorado.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Marigold</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          A great restaurant worth checking out if you have another free night. The
          celeriac &lsquo;parmigiana&rsquo; is one of the best meals Brennan has ever
          had.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── ESTES PARK ── %>
  <div class="mb-20">
    <h2 class="font-serif font-light text-4xl text-nasturtium-forest-dark mb-4">Estes Park</h2>
    <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed mb-6">
      The gateway to Rocky Mountain National Park &mdash; where Brennan does most of
      his backcountry skiing! It&rsquo;ll be a day trip that takes a few hours but
      wow is it beautiful. A number of lookouts along the windy Trail Ridge Road
      provide stunning mountain views even without the need to hike. If you venture
      high enough, you might see some golden aspens this time of year. A true
      bucket-list-worthy sight if you haven&rsquo;t already crossed it off your list.
    </p>
    <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed mb-10">
      Downtown Estes is also a tourist-friendly and quaint day trip from Lyons. The
      drive is up a pretty rock-walled canyon and it is also a windy road in case any
      of you are sensitive to curves while driving in a car (experience tells us that
      a few of you are!).
    </p>

    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-nasturtium-olive mb-5">Food</p>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Antonio&rsquo;s Real New York Pizza</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Yup. You read that right. &ldquo;Real&rdquo; New York pizza in the
          mountains of Colorado. Does it live up to its name? We&rsquo;ll let you
          decide.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Bird &amp; Jim</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          A more upscale place that has incredible food and great cocktails.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Wapiti Colorado Pub</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Outdoor deck sits above the Fall River for a nice outdoor pubby meal. The
          menu features Rocky Mountain Oysters &mdash; you&rsquo;ll learn if you
          don&rsquo;t already know.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── LONGMONT ── %>
  <div>
    <h2 class="font-serif font-light text-4xl text-nasturtium-forest-dark mb-4">Longmont</h2>
    <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed mb-10">
      A suburb of Boulder that provides a more laid back vibe. The Main Street is a
      nice place to walk around with a number of shops and restaurants to check out.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">La Mariposa</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          A popular, rooftop Mexican place that&rsquo;s open late and is a good go-to
          for tacos, apps, and margs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-nasturtium-forest mb-1">Left Hand Brewery</p>
        <p class="text-nasturtium-forest-dark leading-relaxed">
          Another long-standing Colorado brewery that has a spacious beer garden next
          door to the main, old school brewery. The location is off the main drag of
          downtown Longmont and provides beautiful views of Longs Peak, one of 58
          mountain peaks above 14,000 feet in Colorado. Brennan has climbed it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
